   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Anurag,<div><br></div><div>Unfortunately I don&#39;t have have an easy solution for you. Ruslan did some <a href=\"https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/pull/64\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/pull/64&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343511544000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LlCoJT6W4oMux9y_KeLFY\">heroic</a> work to add sourceRefs to the AST but I&#39;ve had to remove most of it because I don&#39;t think we got the srcRef representation right and it led to errors elsewhere.</div><div><br></div><div>Anyway, the only two solutions currently are </div><div>1) Run in debug mode with a Java IDE</div><div>2) Old fashioned println debugging: Add cat(&quot;about to eval source file X.R\\n&quot;) throughout your script to see how far you get.</div><div><br></div><div>If you use a Java IDE, set a breakpoint for EvalException and then look for calls to the &quot;evaluateCall&quot; java method. You can then follow the R stack trace upward.</div><div><br></div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/renjin-dev/attach/2487e2f4ae52b/debug.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"debug.png\" style=\"max-width:100%;opacity:1\"><div><br></div><div>Hope this helps!</div><div><br></div><div>Alex</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
